Providing expert guidance and advice throughout a product's lifecycle shifts the relationship between manufacturer and user from transactional to relational. When consumers understand how to properly use, maintain, and eventually return products, they develop higher engagement and are more likely to participate in circular systems. This strategy recognizes that product longevity and effective reuse depend not only on design quality but on user knowledge and behavior. By offering accessible advice through multiple channels—digital platforms, documentation, training—companies can significantly extend product lifespans and improve return rates.